From 1691b758c40de22193b7dca5972ba3d0e86c69a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 19:28:34 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lane-296 int8 goal stage 9: F32ACC takes <type>:<role> and
 <type>:all; op probe replays any weight type and times widths

- GGML_ARIFI_F32ACC entries may name the weight type (sx8:ffn_down, sx8:all), so f32 accumulation can stay on the
  S-X8 roles and leave the Q4_K_XL / GSQ float paths byte-identical.
- arifi-op-probe: replay any GGUF weight type with a host to_float (S-X8, Q4_K, ...), several items per run, f64
  reference on the reference rows only (output head 248320 rows); `time` mode: per-rep kernel time per width
  (PROBE_NS, PROBE_REPS, warm rep discarded) and an FNV hash of the output for bit identity across variants.
- arifi-op-capture: PROBE_LAYERS filter, non-block roles (output), PROBE_ALL_LOGITS (output head at n=512).
Binary b-int8c relinked 19:21 from this tree (llama-perplexity sha256 fbb62f07...dfd6ab0b, night/ev16/binary-sha256.txt).

Lane: lane-296
